.playwright/
# Cargo build output. Written here with a leading slash so it anchors to the
# repository root. A `router/.gitignore` containing `/target/` would anchor to
# `router/` instead and match nothing, which is how a nested root-anchored
# pattern silently fails.
/router/target/
# Agent worktrees. `git worktree add .worktrees/<name>` creates a full checkout
# per parallel sub-agent, and without this the whole nested tree shows up as
# untracked in every one of them.
.worktrees/
# The root Cargo workspace's build output. Anchored with a leading slash because
# it now lives at the repository root rather than under `router/`.
/target/
